<component name="ProjectRunConfigurationManager">
  <!-- First before-launch step of "SunoMaker (Go debugger)". GoLand compiles that
       config to a fixed path in its tmp dir and overwrites it on every run;
       Windows refuses to overwrite a running image, so one surviving instance
       fails the whole launch with "The process cannot access the file because it
       is being used by another process" — an error about the previous run, not
       about the code, which is what makes it confusing.

       They survive because stopping a Wails debug session kills the parent and
       leaves the webview child behind, windowless, where it accumulates silently.

       **The pattern is scoped to this app by name, and that is load-bearing**
       (#14). GoLand derives the temporary binary's name from the run
       configuration's name, so it is the *config name* that separates one
       project's debug binary from another's — not the path, which is the same
       JetBrains tmp directory for every project on this machine. This was
       originally copied from Site Maker Pro, whose config is called "App (Go
       debugger)", and left matching '___*App__Go_debugger_' — which matched Site
       Maker Pro's session too, so launching SunoMaker under the debugger killed
       it. The config is now "SunoMaker (Go debugger)" and this matches that.

       So: if the debugger config is ever renamed, rename it here in the same
       breath, and never widen this back to a name another project could share.

       The `___<N>` prefix is GoLand's own index and varies per run, hence the
       wildcard. Matched on process name rather than on the path under the
       JetBrains tmp dir so it keeps working when GoLand is upgraded and the
       version in that path moves. A real suno-maker.exe the producer is running
       from build/bin is left alone — it is not named this.

       Always exits 0. A before-launch task that failed when it found nothing to
       kill would block every clean launch. -->
  <configuration default="false" name="Kill stale debug processes" type="ShConfigurationType">
    <option name="SCRIPT_TEXT" value="$p = @(Get-Process -Name '___*SunoMaker__Go_debugger_' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue); if ($p.Count -eq 0) { 'No stale SunoMaker debug processes.' } else { $p | ForEach-Object { Write-Host ('Killing stale PID ' + $_.Id + ' (' + $_.ProcessName + ')') }; $p | Stop-Process -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue; Wait-Process -Id ($p | ForEach-Object { $_.Id }) -Timeout 10 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue }; exit 0" />
    <option name="INDEPENDENT_SCRIPT_PATH" value="true" />
    <option name="SCRIPT_PATH" value="" />
    <option name="SCRIPT_OPTIONS" value="" />
    <option name="INDEPENDENT_SCRIPT_WORKING_DIRECTORY" value="true" />
    <option name="SCRIPT_WORKING_DIRECTORY" value="$PROJECT_DIR$" />
    <option name="INDEPENDENT_INTERPRETER_PATH" value="true" />
    <option name="INTERPRETER_PATH" value="powershell.exe" />
    <option name="INTERPRETER_OPTIONS" value="-NoProfile -Command" />
    <option name="EXECUTE_IN_TERMINAL" value="false" />
    <option name="EXECUTE_SCRIPT_FILE" value="false" />
    <envs />
    <method v="2" />
  </configuration>
</component>
